{
  "feature_instruction": "The Booking System API feature provides backend services and controllers for managing gym classes, trainers, and user bookings. It exposes public endpoints for viewing class schedules and trainer profiles, and authenticated endpoints for users to manage their personal bookings. Additionally, it includes administrative endpoints for full CRUD operations on classes, trainers, and all bookings.\n\n**Data Transfer Objects (DTOs):**\n- `BookingDto`: Represents a booking with `id` (UUID), `userId` (UUID), `gymClass` (GymClassDto), `bookingTime` (LocalDateTime), and `status` (BookingStatus).\n- `GymClassDto`: Represents a gym class with `id` (UUID), `name` (String), `description` (String), `trainer` (TrainerDto), `startTime` (LocalDateTime), `endTime` (LocalDateTime), `capacity` (Integer), and `currentBookings` (Integer).\n- `TrainerDto`: Represents a trainer with `id` (UUID), `name` (String), `bio` (String), `specializations` (String), and `imageUrl` (String).\n- `CreateBookingRequest`: Used for creating a new booking, containing `gymClassId` (UUID) and `userId` (UUID).\n\n**Service Layer:**\n- `BookingService`: Handles the core business logic for bookings. It depends on `BookingRepository` and `GymClassRepository` from the `booking-system-core` feature.\n  - `createBooking(CreateBookingRequest request)`: Creates a new booking. It first validates if the gym class exists and has available capacity. It also checks if the user has an active membership (by calling `membership-management`'s `MembershipService.getUserActiveMemberships`). If the user has no active membership, it throws an `IllegalArgumentException`. If the class is full, it throws an `IllegalStateException`. If the user has already booked this class, it throws an `IllegalStateException`. It then saves the booking and updates the `currentBookings` count for the `GymClass`. Returns `BookingDto`.\n  - `cancelBooking(UUID bookingId)`: Cancels an existing booking. It retrieves the booking, marks it as cancelled, and decrements the `currentBookings` count for the associated `GymClass`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the booking does not exist. Returns `void`.\n  - `getBookingsByUserId(UUID userId)`: Retrieves all bookings for a specific user. Returns `List<BookingDto>`.\n  - `getBookingById(UUID bookingId)`: Retrieves a single booking by its ID. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the booking does not exist. Returns `BookingDto`.\n  - `getAllBookings()`: Retrieves all bookings in the system. Returns `List<BookingDto>`.\n- `GymClassService`: Manages gym class-related business logic. It depends on `GymClassRepository` and `TrainerRepository` from the `booking-system-core` feature.\n  - `getAllGymClasses()`: Retrieves all gym classes. Returns `List<GymClassDto>`.\n  - `getGymClassById(UUID id)`: Retrieves a gym class by its ID. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the class does not exist. Returns `GymClassDto`.\n  - `createGymClass(GymClassDto dto)`: Creates a new gym class. Returns `GymClassDto`.\n  - `updateGymClass(UUID id, GymClassDto dto)`: Updates an existing gym class. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the class does not exist. Returns `GymClassDto`.\n  - `deleteGymClass(UUID id)`: Deletes a gym class. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the class does not exist. Returns `void`.\n  - `getClassesByTrainerId(UUID trainerId)`: Retrieves all classes taught by a specific trainer. Returns `List<GymClassDto>`.\n- `TrainerService`: Manages trainer-related business logic. It depends on `TrainerRepository` from the `booking-system-core` feature.\n  - `getAllTrainers()`: Retrieves all trainers. Returns `List<TrainerDto>`.\n  - `getTrainerById(UUID id)`: Retrieves a trainer by their ID. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the trainer does not exist. Returns `TrainerDto`.\n  - `createTrainer(TrainerDto dto)`: Creates a new trainer. Returns `TrainerDto`.\n  - `updateTrainer(UUID id, TrainerDto dto)`: Updates an existing trainer. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the trainer does not exist. Returns `TrainerDto`.\n  - `deleteTrainer(UUID id)`: Deletes a trainer. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the trainer does not exist. Returns `void`.\n\n**Controller Layer:**\n- `BookingController`: Exposes REST endpoints for authenticated users to manage their bookings. It injects `BookingService`.\n  - `createBooking(CreateBookingRequest request)`: Handles POST requests to `/api/v1/bookings` to create a new booking. Returns `ResponseEntity<BookingDto>` (201 Created on success, 400 Bad Request for validation errors, 404 Not Found if class or user not found, 409 Conflict if class is full or already booked).\n  - `cancelBooking(UUID bookingId)`: Handles DELETE requests to `/api/v1/bookings/{bookingId}` to cancel a booking. Returns `ResponseEntity<Void>` (204 No Content on success, 404 Not Found if booking not found).\n  - `getUserBookings(UUID userId)`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/bookings/users/{userId}` to retrieve all bookings for a specific user. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<BookingDto>>` (200 OK).\n- `GymClassController`: Exposes public REST endpoints for fetching gym class schedules. It injects `GymClassService`.\n  - `getAllGymClasses()`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/gym-classes` to retrieve all gym classes. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<GymClassDto>>` (200 OK).\n  - `getGymClassById(UUID id)`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/gym-classes/{id}` to retrieve a single gym class by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<GymClassDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if class not found).\n- `TrainerController`: Exposes public REST endpoints for fetching trainer profiles. It injects `TrainerService`.\n  - `getAllTrainers()`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/trainers` to retrieve all trainers. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<TrainerDto>>` (200 OK).\n  - `getTrainerById(UUID id)`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/trainers/{id}` to retrieve a single trainer by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<TrainerDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if trainer not found).\n- `AdminBookingController`: Exposes admin REST endpoints for managing all bookings. It injects `BookingService`.\n  - `getAllBookings()`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/admin/bookings` to retrieve all bookings. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<BookingDto>>` (200 OK).\n  - `getBookingById(UUID bookingId)`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/admin/bookings/{bookingId}` to retrieve a single booking by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<BookingDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if booking not found).\n  - `cancelBooking(UUID bookingId)`: Handles DELETE requests to `/api/v1/admin/bookings/{bookingId}` to cancel a booking. Returns `ResponseEntity<Void>` (204 No Content on success, 404 Not Found if booking not found).\n- `AdminGymClassController`: Exposes admin REST endpoints for CRUD operations on gym classes. It injects `GymClassService`.\n  - `getAllGymClasses()`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/admin/gym-classes` to retrieve all gym classes. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<GymClassDto>>` (200 OK).\n  - `getGymClassById(UUID id)`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/admin/gym-classes/{id}` to retrieve a single gym class by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<GymClassDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if class not found).\n  - `createGymClass(GymClassDto dto)`: Handles POST requests to `/api/v1/admin/gym-classes` to create a new gym class. Returns `ResponseEntity<GymClassDto>` (201 Created).\n  - `updateGymClass(UUID id, GymClassDto dto)`: Handles PUT requests to `/api/v1/admin/gym-classes/{id}` to update an existing gym class. Returns `ResponseEntity<GymClassDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if class not found).\n  - `deleteGymClass(UUID id)`: Handles DELETE requests to `/api/v1/admin/gym-classes/{id}` to delete a gym class. Returns `ResponseEntity<Void>` (204 No Content, 404 Not Found if class not found).\n- `AdminTrainerController`: Exposes admin REST endpoints for CRUD operations on trainer profiles. It injects `TrainerService`.\n  - `getAllTrainers()`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/admin/trainers` to retrieve all trainers. Returns `ResponseEntity<List<TrainerDto>>` (200 OK).\n  - `getTrainerById(UUID id)`: Handles GET requests to `/api/v1/admin/trainers/{id}` to retrieve a single trainer by ID. Returns `ResponseEntity<TrainerDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if trainer not found).\n  - `createTrainer(TrainerDto dto)`: Handles POST requests to `/api/v1/admin/trainers` to create a new trainer. Returns `ResponseEntity<TrainerDto>` (201 Created).\n  - `updateTrainer(UUID id, TrainerDto dto)`: Handles PUT requests to `/api/v1/admin/trainers/{id}` to update an existing trainer. Returns `ResponseEntity<TrainerDto>` (200 OK, 404 Not Found if trainer not found).\n  - `deleteTrainer(UUID id)`: Handles DELETE requests to `/api/v1/admin/trainers/{id}` to delete a trainer. Returns `ResponseEntity<Void>` (204 No Content, 404 Not Found if trainer not found).\n\nError handling for all controllers will be managed by `GlobalExceptionHandler` from the `shared-backend` feature, which maps `ResourceNotFoundException` to 404 Not Found and other exceptions to appropriate HTTP status codes.",
