  "feature_instruction": "The Notification Service is responsible for sending various types of email notifications to users based on events within the ABS FITNESS system, such as booking confirmations, membership renewals, and class reminders. It integrates with the booking-system-core and membership-management features to retrieve necessary data for crafting personalized emails. The `NotificationService` class provides methods for sending different types of notifications, while the `ScheduledTasksService` class orchestrates the periodic checking of upcoming events and membership statuses to trigger these notifications.\n\n### NotificationService.java\n\nThis service handles the actual sending of emails. It will have methods for specific notification types:\n\n1.  `sendBookingConfirmationEmail(UUID userId, UUID bookingId)`: This method will fetch the booking details from `booking-system-core` using `BookingService.getBookingById(bookingId)` and user details (if available, otherwise use a placeholder). It will then construct and send an email confirming the booking, including class name, trainer, date, and time. It should return `void`.\n2.  `sendMembershipRenewalReminderEmail(UUID userId, UUID userMembershipId)`: This method will fetch the user membership details from `membership-management` using `MembershipService.getUserActiveMemberships(userId)` and filter for the specific `userMembershipId`. It will then construct and send an email reminding the user about their upcoming membership renewal, including the membership plan name, end date, and a call to action to renew. It should return `void`.\n3.  `sendUpcomingClassReminderEmail(UUID userId, UUID bookingId)`: Similar to the booking confirmation, this method will fetch booking details and send a reminder email for an upcoming class, typically 24 hours before the class starts. It should return `void`.\n\nError Handling: If a booking or membership is not found, a `ResourceNotFoundException` should be thrown.\n\n### 