r will be navigated to the `/account/dashboard` route. On error, a toast notification will display the error message.\n\n### SignupPage.tsx\nThis page will display a signup form with fields for email, password, and confirm password. It will include a prominent heading \"Join the ABS FITNESS Community\" and a call to action button \"Sign Up\". Below the signup form, there will be a link to the login page. The form submission will call `useAuth().signup(email, password)`. On successful signup, the user will be navigated to the `/account/dashboard` route. On error, a toast notification will display the error message.\n\n### ProtectedRoute.tsx\nThis component will receive `children` as props. It will use the `useAuth().isAuthenticated` value to determine if the user is logged in. If `isAuthenticated` is `false`, the user will be redirected to the `/login` page using `react-router-dom`'s `Navigate` component. Otherwise, it will render the `children` components. This component ensures that only authenticated users can access specific routes within the application, such as the member portal.",
