  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A1A1A] text-[#FFFFFF]\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#FF5722] hover:bg-[#E64A19] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#FF5722]\n- Section bg: bg-[#F5F5F5] (odd sections) / bg-white (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-[#1A1A1A] leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature provides the frontend user interface for viewing and purchasing membership plans for ABS FITNESS. It consists of a `MembershipPage` to display all available plans, `MembershipPlanCard` components to render individual plan details, a `CheckoutPage` for the multi-step purchase process, and `OrderSummary` and `PaymentForm` components within the checkout flow. The `membershipService.ts` file handles all API interactions with the backend `membership-management` feature, specifically calling `getAllMembershipPlans` to fetch plans and `purchaseMembership` to complete a transaction. The `membership.ts` file defines the TypeScript types used across this feature.\n\n### MembershipPage.tsx\nThis page is responsible for fetching all active membership plans from the backend using the `membershipService.getAllMembershipPlans()` function. It will display these plans in a grid layout, with each plan rendered by a `MembershipPlanCard` component. The page will have a hero section with a motivational headline and subheadline, followed by a section showcasing the membership plans. Each `MembershipPlanCard` will have a prominent call-to-action button that, when clicked, navigates the user to the `CheckoutPage` with the selected `MembershipPlanDto.id` as a URL parameter.\n\n### MembershipPlanCard.tsx\nThis component receives a `MembershipPlanDto` as a prop and displays its details, including `name`, `durationInMonths`, `price`, and `features`. The price should be formatted in Indian Rupees (₹) using `toLocaleString('en-IN', { style: 'currency', currency: 'INR' })`. It will include a \"Select Plan\" or \"Join Now\" button that triggers navigation to the `CheckoutPage` with the plan's ID. The card design will reflect a premium aesthetic with clear typography and a prominent CTA.\n\n### CheckoutPage.tsx\nThis page orchestrates the multi-step membership purchase process. It will retrieve the `membershipPlanId` from the URL parameters and fetch the corresponding `MembershipPlanDto` using `membershipService.getMembershipPlanById()`. The checkout flow will involve at least two steps: a summary step displaying the selected plan and total cost (rendered by `OrderSummary`), and a payment step (rendered by `PaymentForm`). The `useAuth()` hook will be used to get the current user's `userId` for the `PurchaseMembershipRequest`. Upon successful payment, the `membershipService.purchaseMembership()` function will be called with the `membershipPlanId` and `userId`. The page will display success or error messages using a toast notification system (e.g., `sonner`).\n\n### OrderSummary.tsx\nThis component receives the selected `MembershipPlanDto` as a prop. It displays a clear summary of the membership plan, including its `name`, `durationInMonths`, and `price`. The total amount due will be prominently displayed, formatted in Indian Rupees (₹). It will also include any relevant disclaimers or terms and conditions.\n\n### PaymentForm.tsx\nThis component is responsible for integrating with the payment gateway. It will render a form for payment details. Upon submission, it will call the `membershipService.purchaseMembership()` function with the `membershipPlanId` and `userId`. It should handle loading states and display feedback to the user regarding the payment status. The component will use the `useAuth()` hook to get the current user's `userId`.\n\n### membershipService.ts\nThis service file provides asynchronous functions to interact with the backend `membership-management` API. It will export `getAllMembershipPlans()` to fetch a list of all active membership plans, `getMembershipPlanById(id: UUID)` to fetch a single membership plan by its ID, and `purchaseMembership(request: PurchaseMembershipRequest)` to initiate the purchase of a membership. These functions will use the generated API client to make HTTP requests to the respective backend endpoints.\n\n### membership.ts\nThis file defines the TypeScript interfaces for `MembershipPlanDto` and `PurchaseMembershipRequest` based on the backend `membership-management` feature's `data_shapes`. It will also define any other local types required for the frontend representation of membership data.",
