{
  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A1A1A] text-[#FFFFFF]\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#FF5722] hover:bg-[#E64A19] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#FF5722]\n- Section bg: bg-white (odd sections) / bg-[#F5F5F5] (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-gray-700 leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature implements the member portal for ABS FITNESS, providing a personalized experience for logged-in users to manage their bookings, view membership details, and update their profile. The core of this feature is the `AccountLayout` component, which provides a consistent sidebar navigation and overall structure for all member-specific pages. All pages within this feature (`AccountDashboardPage`, `MyBookingsPage`, `MyMembershipPage`, `ProfilePage`) will utilize this `AccountLayout`.\n\n`AccountLayout` will render a sidebar with navigation links to the dashboard, my bookings, my membership, and profile pages. It will also display the current user's name and email, retrieved from the `useAuth()` hook. The main content area will render the `children` prop, which will be the specific member portal page.\n\n`AccountDashboardPage` will serve as the landing page for the member portal. It will display a welcome message to the user, a summary of their current membership (fetching data using the generated service function `getUserActiveMemberships` from `membership-flow` feature), and a summary of their upcoming bookings (fetching data using the generated service function `getBookingsByUserId` from `booking-ui` feature). It will also include prominent CTAs to view all bookings and manage membership.\n\n`MyBookingsPage` will display a detailed list of all bookings made by the logged-in user. It will fetch booking data using the generated service function `getBookingsByUserId` from `booking-ui` feature. Each booking entry will show the class name, trainer, date, time, and a button to cancel the booking. The cancel booking functionality will call the generated service function `cancelBooking` from `booking-ui` feature. All monetary values will be displayed in Indian Rupees (₹) using the `en-IN` locale.\n\n`MyMembershipPage` will display the user's current and past membership details. It will fetch membership data using the generated service function `getUserActiveMemberships` and `getUserMemberships` from `membership-flow` feature. It will show the membership plan name, start date, end date, and any associated features. All monetary values will be displayed in Indian Rupees (₹) using the `en-IN` locale.\n\n`ProfilePage` will allow members to view and potentially edit their personal profile information. This page will retrieve user information from the `useAuth()` hook. For now, it will display the user's name and email, with placeholder fields for future editing capabilities. No backend calls are required for this initial version beyond what `useAuth()` provides.\n\nAll pages will ensure a professional and results-oriented tone, with clear and empowering messaging for the members.",
