{
  "feature_instruction": "The Notification Service feature is responsible for sending various email notifications to users of ABS FITNESS. It consists of two main services: `NotificationService` which handles the actual email sending logic, and `ScheduledTasksService` which orchestrates scheduled jobs to trigger these notifications. This feature integrates with the `booking-system-core` and `membership-management` features to retrieve necessary data for notifications.\n\n## NotificationService.java\nThis service contains the core logic for constructing and sending different types of emails. It will inject `BookingService` from `booking-system-core` and `MembershipService` from `membership-management` to fetch details required for email content. It will use a placeholder email sending mechanism (e.g., `System.out.println` for demonstration purposes, or a simple mail sender if available in the scaffolded project).\n\n### public void sendBookingConfirmationEmail(UUID userId, UUID bookingId)\n1. Fetch `BookingDto` using `bookingService.getBookingById(bookingId)`. If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n2. Extract `GymClassDto` and `TrainerDto` details from the `BookingDto`.\n3. Construct an email subject: \"ABS FITNESS: Your Booking Confirmation for {GymClassName}\".\n4. Construct an email body including user ID, gym class name, trainer name, start time, and end time.\n5. Log the email content to console (or send via mail sender).\n\n### public void sendMembershipRenewalReminderEmail(UUID userId, UUID userMembershipId)\n1. Fetch `UserMembershipDto` using `membershipService.getUserActiveMemberships(userId)` and filter by `userMembershipId`. If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n2. Extract `MembershipPlanDto` details from the `UserMembershipDto`.\n3. Construct an email subject: \"ABS FITNESS: Your Membership Renewal Reminder\".\n4. Construct an email body including user ID, membership plan name, start date, and end date.\n5. Log the email content to console (or send via mail sender).\n\n### public void sendUpcomingClassReminderEmail(UUID userId, UUID bookingId)\n1. Fetch `BookingDto` using `bookingService.getBookingById(bookingId)`. If not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n2. Extract `GymClassDto` and `TrainerDto` details from the `BookingDto`.\n3. Construct an email subject: \"ABS FITNESS: Reminder for Your Upcoming Class - {GymClassName}\".\n4. Construct an email body including user ID, gym class name, trainer name, start time, and end time.\n5. Log the email content to console (or send via mail sender).\n\n## ScheduledTasksService.java\nThis service will contain `@Scheduled` methods to periodically check for upcoming events and trigger the appropriate notification emails via `NotificationService`. It will inject `NotificationService`, `BookingService`, and `MembershipService`.\n\n### public void scheduleUpcomingClassReminders()\n1. This method will be scheduled to run daily (e.g., at 8 AM).\n2. Calculate a time window for upcoming classes (e.g., classes starting in the next 24-48 hours).\n3. Call `gymClassRepository.findByStartTimeBetweenOrderByStartTimeAsc(start, end)` to get relevant `GymClass` entities.\n4. For each `GymClass`, retrieve all `Booking` entities using `bookingRepository.findByGymClassId(gymClass.getId())`.\n5. For each `Booking`, call `notificationService.sendUpcomingClassReminderEmail(booking.getUserId(), booking.getId())`.\n6. Implement appropriate logging for scheduled task execution and email sending.\n\n### public void scheduleMembershipRenewalReminders()\n1. This method will be scheduled to run weekly (e.g., every Monday at 9 AM).\n2. Calculate a date window for expiring memberships (e.g., memberships expiring in the next 7-14 days).\n3. Call `userMembershipRepository.findByEndDateBetween(start, end)` to get relevant `UserMembership` entities.\n4. For each `UserMembership`, call `notificationService.sendMembershipRenewalReminderEmail(userMembership.getUserId(), userMembership.getId())`.\n5. Implement appropriate logging for scheduled task execution and email sending.",
